This is a real Linux kernel (6.6, built for i386) with BusyBox as the
userland, booted from a single bzImage file by the v86 emulator.
The whole system is an initramfs in RAM.

Things to try:
  uname -a          kernel version
  cat /proc/cpuinfo the emulated CPU
  free -m           memory
  top               processes (q quits)
  vi notes.txt      the vi editor (Esc then :wq saves)
  doom              opens DOOM in a window over this screen
